            <h2>Train Duration, Distance, and Travel Time Overview</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Baltimore to New Haven covers roughly 239 miles (385 km) along the busy Northeast Corridor, linking two of the East Coast’s most historic cities. Although this isn’t a high speed rail corridor like in Europe, Amtrak’s Acela and Northeast Regional trains offer a steady and pleasant pace, often making the trip more enjoyable than a long drive.</p>


