            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>1. How long is the train from Baltimore to New Haven?</h3>
            <p>The train journey typically takes 4 hours 9 minutes to 5 hours 30 minutes, depending on the service and the number of stops.</p>


            <h3>2. What is the fastest train from Baltimore to New Haven?</h3>
            <p>The fastest option is Amtrak Acela, which can complete the journey in approximately 4 hours and 9 minutes with direct service.</p>



            <h3>3. How much does a train ticket from Baltimore to New Haven cost?</h3>
            <p>
                Ticket prices generally fall between:
                $39-$70 for early booking on the Northeast Regional Coach
                $70-$120 for standard Northeast Regional fares
                $90-$180 for Northeast Regional Business
                $150-$350+ for Acela Business
                $250-$500+ for Acela First or last-minute travel
            </p>



            <h3>4. Are there direct trains from Baltimore to New Haven?</h3>
            <p>Yes, most Amtrak Northeast Regional, Acela, and Vermonter trains are direct, so there’s no need for transfers.</p>



            <h3>5. What amenities are available onboard?</h3>
            <p>Trains offer comfortable seating, Wi-Fi (where available), power outlets, a café car, and luggage space. Acela adds premium seating, at-seat meal service (First Class), and priority boarding.</p>



            <h3>6. Is train travel faster than driving?</h3>
            <p>Depending on traffic, driving may take 4-5 hours, while the train is generally stress-free, predictable, and allows productive travel time.</p>



            <h3>7. Can you travel from Baltimore to New Haven in one day?</h3>
            <p>Yes, the route is suitable for same-day trips, with early departures allowing a full day in New Haven.</p>



            <h3>8. Which station in Baltimore do trains depart from?</h3>
            <p>Most trains depart from Baltimore Penn Station, located in downtown Baltimore. Some connections are available from BWI Airport Station.</p>



            <h3>9. Which station do trains arrive at in New Haven?</h3>
            <p>Trains arrive at New Haven Union Station, conveniently located in the city center and easily accessible by Metro-North, CT Rail, and local buses.</p>



            <h3>10. Is Business Class or Acela worth it?</h3>
            <p>Yes, Business Class offers extra legroom and a quieter environment. At the same time, Acela provides the fastest journey with premium amenities, making both ideal for travelers seeking more comfort during the 4-5 hour journey.</p>











